data.content:
It works. Here's the key detail:

**`JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase`** is a built-in policy added in .NET 11. Since your record uses lowercase parameter names (`name`, `age`), the generated properties are also lowercase by default. The `PascalCase` policy converts them to `Name` and `Age` in the JSON output — no custom code needed.

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("Alice", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase,
    WriteIndented = true
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string name, int age);
```

Output:

```json
{
  "Name": "Alice",
  "Age": 30
}
```
